message: "If you use this skill, or adapt its scoring model, please cite it as below."
title: "model-router: a two-axis Claude model and effort router"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Saigal"
    given-names: "Rishav"
    email: "rishavsaigal@gmail.com"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-5548-3016"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Rishav1996/model-router"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.2
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21520842"
date-released: 2026-07-24
abstract: >
  A Claude Code / Claude API skill that recommends the cheapest Claude model
  and effort level that will still get a task right on the first try, by
  scoring capability requirements (a maximum over depth, stakes, and
  agentic-loop complexity) and cost exposure (a sum over context, output, and
  agentic-loop complexity) as two separate axes instead of one blended
  complexity score.
keywords:
  - claude
  - claude-code
  - model-routing
  - cost-optimization
  - llm
  - anthropic
